    // Use an input flag `callPlay` to decide whether to attempt to call play(); if play() returns (does not revert), we observe balances before/after and assert
    // the stated invariant. The test will attempt to make play succeed when possible (i.e., if timestamps were set earlier by some other actor), but the invariant
    // must hold for ALL inputs. We implement robust checking: if play reverted then the assert requires that reverted==true implies nothing about balances;
    // but when play did NOT revert, we check the stated balance decrease property.

